## Bythos

A bythos is tall and gaunt, and where its face should be there is a pit with nothing in it. Looking into that pit muddles the mind. The creature keeps its own time: it quickens itself so that it moves and strikes faster than those around it, and it can lay a sluggishness on someone else, holding them slow while it moves freely. A blow from a bythos shoves a person out of the present, so that they vanish and come back a few moments later to find the fight already ended around them. It mends its own wounds as it stands.

Two bythos guarded the garden of the [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Gilded Spire/index|Gilded Spire]] on [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]], beside the [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Gilded Spire/Wriggling Man|Wriggling Man]] and a pair of [[Bestiary/Fiends#Astra Demon|Astra Demons]]. Both are dead.
